00:00:00.030 --> 00:00:01.670 align:start position:0%
 
more than three months ago House  Majority Whip Steve Scalise miraculously  survived an attempt to assassinate GOP  lawmakers on a baseball field in  Virginia today he returned to the job  for the first time since the shooting in  a packed house chamber filled with joy  then the Louisiana congressman delivered  an emotional address to his colleagues  Thank You mr. speaker  you have no idea how great this feels to  be back here at work in the people's  house when I was laying out on that ball  field the first thing I did once I was  down and I couldn't move anymore  as I just started to pray and I will  tell you it gave me an unbelievable  sense of calm knowing that at that point  it was in God's hands a lot of people  asked did this event change you yes it  changed me but not in the ways you might  think it's it's only strengthened my  faith in God and it's really  crystallized what what shows up as the  goodness in people I got to see that  goodness in people  Scalise thanked the Capitol Hill  officers who saved his life and  countless of others that day in June and  then he had a personal message for all  the lawmakers in that room when I come  back into this chamber here today it  just see in the faces of all of you it  just means more to me than you can  imagine so thanks for all of that love  and support we are the people's house  this is the place where these ideas are  supposed to be debated and we fight  through those issues but ultimately we  come together on whatever the board  shows us 218 if you can put the majority  together  that's what rules the day it's so  important that is we're having those  political battles we don't make them  personal I am so honored to be back here  in the house serving with you god bless  each and every one of you and god bless  the United States of America what a  special moment and a man who really just  fought for his life there were moments  there was very touch-and-go where people  really thought he wasn't going to make  it but he said through faith and prayer  and the courageousness dana of those  officers putting their life on the line  to be able to save him and the other  lawmakers truly a powerful moment I  think in a really impactful message to  say you know respect to our differences  we can debate  ultimately we have this system of  governance and incredible work also by  the healthcare workers the doctors and  nurses like the emergency room but also  the rehabilitation because it really our  news cycles go so fast it's hard to hear  this was actually only a two and a half  months ago Wow that the shooting took  place and of course it was so traumatic  and remember when President Trump and  mrs. and the first lady go to the  hospital to visit the question was was  he going to make it and the injury could  have severed an artery and this story  would not be as wonderful it is as it is  today so yes I think an amazing return  and you can see his colleagues all seem  genuinely happy to have him back and our  own Lauren fine who used to work here as  a producer is now his communicate as  press secretary for the Majority Whip  and has been working hard to make this  moment happen I thought it was flawless  it was fantastic so she did a wonderful  job it must have been her time here with  us on the five a great powerful moment  and you know he brings up the message  that you know that capital officers  saved his life and you know I have to  tell you thank God that they were armed  and there to be able to protect them  it's also amazing how strong he sounds  after two and a half months you know it  point it points out a really strange sad  reason for him being alive was that the  surgeons were able to save a gunshot  victim because they're so good at it now  I mean they've got a lot of practice in  DC and another good cut in other states  working on gunshot victims in the and it  reminds you the numbers of gunshot  victims could victims could be much  worse than they are now but it's being  covered by the fact that they're the  sturgeons are so good at saving lives  imagine the numbers of Chicago or in DC  so it's not a reduction really in  homicides but surgeons in tech  technology reducing murder so that's  kind of amazing to your point our new  cycle this thing would have been a huge  huge deal for a year yeah but it's like  seems like it happened up forever ago  because we're so constantly churning  through stories you know it's  unbelievable so happy to see my bet and  his family to my goodness so nice yeah  it was a powerful home and I'm not the  most devout guy but when he's talking  about prayer he's talking about people  coming together you just get the chills  running up and  down your spine he wasn't supposed to  survive that was a gunshot wound and  part of the body that's not really  supposed to sustain bullets like that  and he fought back now gabby giffords  also shot in the head I fought back  recovered bravely we talked about on 911  the anniversary the United flight 93  people that storm the cockpit or when  you look at Harvey people wrestling  other Americans out of the water into  safety it's those moments where you  really see the fighting American spirit  and it inspires people it inspires you  to come together as a fellow American  but now these moments are so few and far  between you we were united after 9/11  for a while and then Iraq tore us apart  the Scalise shooting a couple months ago  we had that moment where we reflected  about our rhetoric that's gone  especially after Charlottesville then  Harvey hit and we looked at the Texas  resilience and then now of a sudden  we're talking about the divisive nough  Sonny lers so people just need to  recognize this country is much stronger  when we're together and not divided  alright so the message of unity I've  wanted healthy discussion and debate  that ultimately at the end of the day if  you can put 218 up and the majority will  rule but you know we can respect each  other in that debate process along the  way well absolutely I think that's  what's I hope that's the message people  take away from this because I think we  need more of it and oftentimes it seems  like you know division and anger rule  the day but in what it comes down to is  I think Americans do honor each other  and I love that when Scalise he did an  interview with 60 minutes yes in which  he talked about what the doctors did for  him at MedStar Washington Hospital  Center and he said in very humorous  terms they put Humpty Dumpty back  together again because he described all  the damage in that pelvic area and how  you know in fact he then later had an  infection and it took a lot of work and  a lot of time so looking at him knowing  him I can see he's lost weight but I  thought he looked much better than I  would ever have guessed I thought he was  going to look like a shell but no it  looks like Steve Scalise is still in  there and his spirits stronger than ever  he's a good Majority Whip yes in terms  of his his skills at being able to get  lawmakers to be all on the same page and  the president's gonna need that going  into the tax reform debate and I hope  they listen  a little bit extra closely now at this  point well god bless him and his family  and as Dana said the you know men and  women that saved his life in the  hospital and the capital officers as  well

